.DS_Store
.env
backend/.venv/
backend/*.db
# Copies taken before a migration: useful locally, never part of the history.
/shiftleft.db.backup-*

# The local database travels with the code: it is where connector configuration, project settings
# and the Feature Kickoff defaults live, and losing them on every copy to another machine was
# worse than the noise of a binary file in git. Startup reconciles its schema, so a database from
# an older checkout upgrades itself rather than failing.
#
# Credentials do not travel with it. Every secret in there is Fernet ciphertext, and the key that
# decrypts it is the untracked file below - generated per machine, never committed. On a new
# machine those values cannot be read, so each connector reports "No credential stored" until
# someone enters the token again. That is deliberate: a credential should exist only on the
# machine it was typed into. Never commit .vault_key, and never set SHIFTLEFT_VAULT_ENCRYPTION_KEY
# anywhere tracked - either one turns the ciphertext above back into readable secrets.
backend/.vault_key
backend/**/__pycache__/
backend/.pytest_cache/
backend/.ruff_cache/
backend/*.egg-info/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.angular/
